#{[17592186199519 :tutorial/content "Two statements are **logically equivalent** if they have identical truth tables. \n\nA trivial logical equivalence is that every statement is logically equivalent to itself. We write this as follows:\n\n$$\nP \\equiv P\n$$\n\nTo prove this, we can use a truth table.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,P\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,P\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nSince $P$ and $P$ have identical truth values, they're logically equivalent.\n\nAnother trivial equivalence is that the conjunction of a statement with itself is equivalent to the original statement.\n\n$$\nP \\land P \\equiv P\n$$\n\nFor example, the compound statement \"$x=3$ and $x=3$\" is logically equivalent to \"$x=3$\", which matches our intuition. \n\nAgain, we can prove the general result using a truth table.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,P\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,P\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,P \\land P\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe statements $P$ and $P\\land P$ are logically equivalent since they have identical truth values. \n\nWe also have the following logical equivalence for the disjunction of $P$ with itself.\n\n$$\nP \\lor P \\equiv P\n$$\n\nWe can justify this result using a truth table. \n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,P\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,P\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,P \\lor P\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe statements $P$ and $P\\lor P$ are logically equivalent since they have identical truth values. \n\nCollectively, the results\n\n$$\nP\\land P \\equiv P ,\\qquad P\\lor P \\equiv P\n$$\n\nare known as the **idempotent laws.**"] [17592186199531 :tutorial/content "Recall that a statement $\\beta$ *follows* from statements $\\alpha_1, \\alpha_2, \\ldots, \\alpha_n$ if $\\beta$ is true whenever *all* of $\\alpha_1, \\alpha_2, \\ldots, \\alpha_n$ are true. This is called a *logical inference*.\n\nLet's consider another logical inference rule known as **disjunctive syllogism** (**disjunction elimination** or simply **elimination**). We can state this rule as follows:\n\n$$\nP∨Q; ¬P; ∴Q\n$$\n\nThis rule reads as follows:\n\n> *We have $P \\lor Q$ and $\\lnot P$. Therefore, $Q$.*\n\nTo check that the rule is valid, we can use a truth table:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">Premise 1</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">Premise 2</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">Conclusion</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$P$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$Q$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$P \\lor Q$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\lnot P$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$Q$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">$\\color{blue} \\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">$\\color{blue} \\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">$\\color{red} \\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nBoth $P \\lor Q$ and $\\lnot P$ have the truth value ${\\color{blue}\\mathrm{T}}$ (true) only in the third row of the table. For this row, $Q$ is also ${\\color{red}\\mathrm{T}}$ (true). So, according to the definition, we have a logical inference.\n\nSince disjunction is commutative and the order of the premises does not matter, we have the following variants of the rule:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{l}P \\lor  Q \\\\ \\mathrm{\\neg } P \\\\ \\hline ∴ \\hspace{0.222em} Q\\end{array}}\n\\qquad\\qquad\n\n{\\begin{array}{l}P \\lor  Q \\\\ \\mathrm{\\neg } Q \\\\ \\hline ∴ \\hspace{0.222em} P\\end{array}}\n\\qquad\\qquad\n\n{\\begin{array}{l}\\mathrm{\\neg } P \\\\ P \\lor  Q \\\\ \\hline ∴ \\hspace{0.222em} Q\\end{array}}\n\\qquad\\qquad\n\n{\\begin{array}{l}\\mathrm{\\neg } Q \\\\ P \\lor  Q \\\\ \\hline ∴ \\hspace{0.222em} P\\end{array}}\n$$"] [17592186199532 :tutorial/content "Let's now consider another logical inference rule called **denying the consequent** (or **modus tollens** in Latin):\n\n$$\nP⇒Q; ¬Q; ∴¬P\n$$\n\nIt reads as follows:\n\n> *We have $P \\Rightarrow Q$ and $\\lnot Q$. Therefore, $\\lnot P$.*\n\nWe can use a truth table to check that the rule is valid.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">Premise 1</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">Premise 2</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">Conclusion</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$P$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$Q$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$P \\Rightarrow Q$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\lnot Q$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\lnot P$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">$\\color{blue} \\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">$\\color{blue} \\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">$\\color{red} \\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nBoth $P \\Rightarrow Q$ and $\\lnot Q$ have the truth value ${\\color{blue}\\mathrm{T}}$ (true) only in the fourth row of the table. For this row, $\\lnot P$ also has truth value ${\\color{red}\\mathrm{T}}$ (true). So, according to the definition, we have a logical inference.\n\nSince the order of the premises does not matter, we have the following variants of the rule:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{l}P \\Rightarrow  Q \\\\ \\mathrm{\\neg } Q \\\\ \\hline ∴ \\mathrm{\\neg } P\\end{array}}\n\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\n\n{\\begin{array}{l}\\mathrm{\\neg } Q \\\\ P \\Rightarrow  Q \\\\ \\hline ∴ \\mathrm{\\neg } P\\end{array}}\n$$"] [17592186199533 :tutorial/content "Another important rule of logical inference is called **transitivity of implication** (**chain argument** or **hypothetical syllogism**):\n\n$$\nP⇒Q; Q⇒R; ∴P⇒R\n$$\n\nThis rule is read as follows:\n\n> *We have $P \\Rightarrow Q$ and $Q \\Rightarrow R$. Therefore, $P \\Rightarrow R$.*\n\nWe can use a truth table to check this rule is valid:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">Premise 1</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">Premise 2</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">Conclusion</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$P$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$Q$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$R$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$P \\Rightarrow Q$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$Q \\Rightarrow R$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$P \\Rightarrow R$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">${\\color{blue}\\mathrm{T}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">${\\color{blue}\\mathrm{T}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">${\\color{red}\\mathrm{T}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">${\\color{blue}\\mathrm{T}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">${\\color{blue}\\mathrm{T}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">${\\color{red}\\mathrm{T}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">${\\color{blue}\\mathrm{T}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">${\\color{blue}\\mathrm{T}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">${\\color{red}\\mathrm{T}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">${\\color{blue}\\mathrm{T}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">${\\color{blue}\\mathrm{T}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">${\\color{red}\\mathrm{T}}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nBoth $P \\Rightarrow Q$ and $Q \\Rightarrow R$ have the truth value ${\\color{blue}\\mathrm{T}}$ (true) in the first, fifth, seventh, and eighth rows of the table only. For these rows, $P \\Rightarrow R$ also has the truth value ${\\color{red}\\mathrm{T}}$ (true). So, according to the definition, we have a logical inference.\n\nSince the order of the premises does not matter, we have the following variants of the rule:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{l}P \\Rightarrow  Q \\\\ Q \\Rightarrow  R \\\\ \\hline ∴ \\hspace{0.222em} P \\Rightarrow  R\\end{array}}\n\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\n\n{\\begin{array}{l}Q \\Rightarrow  R \\\\ P \\Rightarrow  Q \\\\ \\hline ∴ \\hspace{0.222em} P \\Rightarrow  R\\end{array}}\n$$"] [17592186199600 :tutorial/content "The statement \"$A$ or $B$,\" represented symbolically as $A \\lor B,$ is true if $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or both $A$ and $B$ are true. Otherwise, it is false. \n\nThe corresponding truth table is shown below:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A \\lor B\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nAs we'll see, truth tables provide a convenient way to determine the truth values of complex logical statements. They can also be used to prove some mathematical theorems!"] [17592186199601 :tutorial/content "Consider the following statement:\n\n$$\nA \\land (B\\lor A)\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can use a truth table to calculate the truth values of this statement given all possible permutations of the truth values of $A$ and $B.$\n\nFirst, we complete a truth table for the part in parentheses, $B \\lor A.$  The statement $B \\lor A$ is true if either $A$ is true, $B$ is true, or both $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B \\lor A\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nNext, we add a new column for $A \\land (B\\lor A).$ \n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B \\lor A\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A \\land (B \\lor A)\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTo fill in the rows, we consider the truth values of $A$ and $(B\\lor A)$ and use this to determine the truth value of $A \\land (B\\lor A)$ in each case.\n\n- Consider the first row. Since $A$ is true and $(B\\lor A)$ is true, their conjunction $A \\land (B\\lor A)$ is *true*:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B \\lor A\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A \\land (B \\lor A)\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\n- Next, consider the second row. Since $A$ is true and $(B\\lor A)$ is true, their conjunction $A \\land (B\\lor A)$ is *true*:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B \\lor A\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A \\land (B \\lor A)\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\n- Now, consider the third row. Since $A$ is false and $(B\\lor A)$ is true, their conjunction $A \\land (B\\lor A)$ is *false*:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B \\lor A\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A \\land (B \\lor A)\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\n- Finally, consider the fourth row. Since $A$ is false and $(B\\lor A)$ is false, their conjunction $A \\land (B\\lor A)$ is *false*:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B \\lor A\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A \\land (B \\lor A)\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe completed truth table is shown below:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,B \\lor A\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,A \\land (B \\lor A)\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186199609 :tutorial/content "The first logical inference rule we'll study is called **implication elimination** (or **modus ponens** in Latin). It states the following:\n\n> *If $P \\Rightarrow Q$ and $P$ are both true, then $Q$ must be also true.*\n\nTo understand this rule, we consider the corresponding truth table:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">Premise 1</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">Premise 2</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">Conclusion</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$P$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$Q$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$P \\Rightarrow Q$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$P$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$Q$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">$\\color{blue} \\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">$\\color{blue} \\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FFE4B5\">$\\color{red} \\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nBoth $P \\Rightarrow Q$ and $P$ have truth value ${\\color{blue}\\mathrm{T}}$ (true) only in the first row of the table. For this row, $Q$ is also ${\\color{red}\\mathrm{T}}$ (true). So, according to our definition, we have a logical inference.\n\nAn alternative way of writing the rule is\n\n$$\nP⇒Q; P; ∴Q\n$$\n\nwhere the symbol $\\,\\raise{1pt}{\\therefore}\\,$ reads as \"therefore\". So, the entire thing reads as follows:\n\n> *We have $P \\Rightarrow Q$ and $P$. Therefore, $Q$.*\n\nSince the order of the premises does not matter, we have the following variants of the rule:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{array}{l}P \\Rightarrow  Q \\\\ P \\\\ \\hline ∴ Q\\end{array}}\n\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad\n\n{\\begin{array}{l}P \\\\ P \\Rightarrow  Q \\\\ \\hline ∴ Q\\end{array}}\n$$"] [17592186203662 :question/problem "A math teacher believes that his students obtain higher algebra scores than geometry. In a geometry test, $2$ out of $10$ students obtain the maximum score. Let $X$ represent the number of students obtaining the maximum score in an algebra test in a sample of $10$ students. Under the null hypothesis that the proportion of students that obtain the maximum score in algebra is the same as in geometry, what is the critical region of a one-tailed test at a significance level of $5\\%$?\n\n*Hint: You may use the table below, representing the **cumulative distribution function** of $X$ under the null hypothesis.*\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-cell-align=\"center\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\quad x \\quad$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$P(X\\leq x)$</td><td>$\\,0.1074\\,$</td>\n<td>$\\,0.3758\\,$</td>\n<td>$\\,0.6778\\,$</td>\n<td>$\\,0.8791\\,$</td>\n<td>$\\,0.9672\\,$</td>\n<td>$\\,0.9936\\,$</td>\n<td>$\\quad\\cdots\\quad$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186203663 :question/problem "A magician has a $6$-sided die, and an audience member suspects it is biased towards landing on $1$. Let $X$ represent the number of times the die lands on $1$ when rolled a total of $5$ times. Under the null hypothesis that the die is fair, what is the critical value of a one-tailed test at a significance level of $2.5\\%$?\n\n*Hint: You may use the table below, representing the **probability mass function** of $X$ under the null hypothesis.*\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\, 0 \\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\, 1 \\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\, 2 \\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\, 3 \\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\, 4 \\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\, 5 \\,$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$P(X=x)$</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\, 0.4019\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\, 0.4019\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\, 0.1608\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\, 0.0322\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\, 0.0032\\,$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\, 0.0001\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186203664 :question/problem "A shop owner believes customer numbers have increased in the last month. Last month, there were $2.5$ customers per hour on average. Let $X$ represent the number of customers visiting the shop in a randomly selected one-hour period. Under the null hypothesis that the number of customers is the same as before, what is the critical region of a one-tailed test at a significance level of $2\\%$?\n\n*Hint: You may use the table below, representing the **probability mass function** of $X$ under the null hypothesis. You may assume that, under the null hypothesis, $P(X \\geq 11) = 0$.*\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\" data-cell-align=\"center\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\quad x \\quad$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\quad\\cdots\\quad$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$P(X= x)$</td>\n<td>$\\quad\\cdots\\quad$</td>\n<td>$\\,0.0668\\,$</td>\n<td>$\\,0.0278\\,$</td>\n<td>$\\,0.0099\\,$</td>\n<td>$\\,0.0031\\,$</td>\n<td>$\\,0.0009\\,$</td>\n<td>$\\,0.0002\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186203665 :question/problem "![](images/7d/7d83475c5477d63fd62d4468d51c88c47451ce56defd06f31524889679ffc7e3.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $J_1$ and $L_1$ are the midpoints of $\\overline{KL}$ and $\\overline{JK}$, respectively.\n\nNow, consider the following statement:\n\n> $J_1L_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} JL$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of this statement. Fill in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></th>\n<th data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Statement</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Reason</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">1</td>\n<td>$J_1$ is the midpoint of $\\overline{KL}$</td>\n<td>Given</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">2</td>\n<td>$KJ_1 = \\dfrac12 KL$</td>\n<td>Definition of a midpoint</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">3</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>Multiplication principle</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">4</td>\n<td>$L_1$ is the midpoint of $\\overline{JK}$</td>\n<td>Given</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">5</td>\n<td>$KL_1 = \\dfrac12 JK$</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">6</td>\n<td>$\\dfrac{KL_1}{JK} = \\dfrac{1}{2}$</td>\n<td>Multiplication principle</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">7</td>\n<td>$\\dfrac{KL_1}{KJ} = \\dfrac{KJ_1}{KL}$</td>\n<td>Transitive property of equality</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">8</td>\n<td>$\\angle{JKL} \\cong \\angle{L_1KJ_1}$</td>\n<td>Reflexive property of congruence</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">9</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>SAS similarity criterion</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">10</td>\n<td>$\\dfrac{J_1L_1}{JL} = \\dfrac{KJ_1}{KL}$</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">11</td>\n<td>$\\dfrac{J_1L_1}{JL} = \\dfrac{1}{2}$</td>\n<td>Transitive property of equality</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">12</td>\n<td>$J_1L_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} JL$</td>\n<td>Multiplication principle</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186203686 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\bigstar$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\maltese$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe adjacency matrix of the relation $R,$ defined over the sets $\\{ 3, 4, 5 \\}$ and $\\{ \\bigstar, \\maltese \\},$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nI. $(4, \\bigstar)$\n\nII. $(5, \\maltese)$\n\nIII. $(3, \\maltese)$"] [17592186203696 :question/problem "Consider the sets $A = \\{2,4,6\\}$ and $B= \\big\\{ \\{1,6\\}, \\{2,3\\}, \\mathbb{N}\\big\\},$ and the relation $R = \\{ (x,y) \\in A \\times B \\::\\: x \\in y \\}.$\nFill in the missing values in the adjacency matrix of the relation:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\{1,6\\}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\{2,3\\}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\mathbb{N}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{0}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{0}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{0}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{1}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{0}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{1}}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186203696 :question/worked-solution "If a relation $R$ is defined over $A = \\{ a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_m \\}$ and $B = \\{ b_1, b_2, \\ldots b_n \\}$ of cardinalities $m$ and $n,$ respectively, the *adjacency matrix* of $R$ is a $m \\times n$-matrix (table), where the element $r_{ij}$ at the intersection of the $i$th row and the $j$th column is given by\n$$\nr_{ij} =\n{\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}1 , \\hspace{1em} \\text{if } {a_i \\: R \\: b_j} , \\\\ 0 , \\hspace{1em} \\text{otherwise} .\\end{array} \\right. }\n$$\n\nThe relation $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y) \\in A \\times B$ with $x \\in y.$\n\nLet's consider each row in our table.\n\n- If $x = 2,$ then the values $y=\\{2,3\\}$ and $y= \\mathbb{N}$ satisfy $x \\in y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(2,\\{2,3\\})$ and $(2,\\mathbb{N}),$ and we write $1$ in the intersection of the $1$st row and the $2$nd column and in the intersection of the $1$st row and the $3$rd column in the adjacency matrix.\n\n- If $x = 4,$ then the value $y = \\mathbb{N}$ satisfies $x \\in y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $\\big(4, \\mathbb{N} \\big),$ and we write $1$ in the intersection of the $2$nd row and the $3$rd column in the adjacency matrix.\n\n- If $x = 6,$ then the values $y=\\{1,6\\}$ and $y= \\mathbb{N}$ satisfy $x \\in y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(6,\\{1,6\\})$ and $(6,\\mathbb{N}),$ and we write $1$ in the intersection of the $3$rd row and the $1$st column and in the intersection of the $3$rd row and the $3$rd column in the adjacency matrix.\n\nAll the other cells in the matrix must be filled with zeros. Therefore, we have the following adjacency matrix:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\{1,6\\}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\{2,3\\}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\mathbb{N}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186203706 :question/problem "Consider a relation $R$ defined on the set $A = \\{ 1, 4, 9\\}.$ Given that $R$ is symmetric, enter the missing values in the corresponding adjacency matrix below. \n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$9$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\phantom{1}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\phantom{1}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\phantom{1}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\phantom{1}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186203706 :question/worked-solution "First, recall the following definitions:\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *symmetric* if for all $x,y \\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\in R \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad (y,x) \\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if a pair $(x,y)$ belongs to a symmetric relation, then the pair $(y,x)$ should also be in the relation.\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *antisymmetric* if for all $x,y \\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\in R \\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad (y,x) \\in R \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x=y.\n$$\n\nIn other words, only one of the pairs, either $(x,y)$ or $(y,x),$ can be in an antisymmetric relation. Note that this condition allows pairs of the form $(x,x).$\n\nWe are given elements of the adjacency matrix in the following highlighted cells outside the main diagonal:  \n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$9$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\phantom{1}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\phantom{1}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\phantom{1}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"Moccasin\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\phantom{1}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"Moccasin\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"Moccasin\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nAs a result, the relation contains the pairs $(9,1)$ and $(9,4).$ Since $R$ is be symmetric, we require \n\n$$\n(1,9) \\in R, \\qquad (4,9) \\in  R.\n$$\n\nSo, the cells corresponding to these elements must all equal $1.$\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$9$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\phantom{1}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\phantom{1}}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"Moccasin\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"Moccasin\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"Moccasin\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nAlso, note the following:\n\n- The symmetric relation condition is equivalent to $(x,y)\\notin R \\Longrightarrow (y,x) \\notin R.$ Therefore, $(4,1)\\notin R$ implies $(1,4) \\notin R.$\n\n- We do not have enough information to determine whether $(1,1)$ is an element of $R.$\n\nLet's add this information to our table.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$9$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}?}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"Moccasin\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"Moccasin\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"Moccasin\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186203717 :question/problem "Complete the following multiplication table for $\\mathbb Z_6$. Use the smallest nonnegative representative for each resulting class.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\times$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=